<task id="036" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Task write tools: spaarke_create_task, spaarke_complete_task (idempotent)</title>
    <phase>2 Long-running work, AI, widgets, task writes</phase>
    <gate>r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Model-callable writes to sprk_event through task 006's capability; idempotency; tags include tenant-isolation</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Thin write adapters over IEventsCapability (006, opus) whose create/complete authorization and must-not-leak proofs already exist; idempotency follows r1's CompleteDecisionTool</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>H</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Tasks/{Create,Complete}TaskTool.cs; the Tasks ledger partial was last edited by 025 (Phase 1, merged)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>006, 020, 025</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, tenant-isolation, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add two model-callable, reversible MCP write tools over task 006's IEventsCapability: spaarke_create_task (POST /api/v1/events semantics, with an idempotency key) and spaarke_complete_task (POST /api/v1/events/{id}/complete, idempotent). Run as the caller; server-side validation is the capability's; a retried create with the same key creates one record.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in the Spaarke Dataverse write path and MCP tool handlers.</role>
  <goal>Create and complete behave as REST for the same caller, are refused with REST reasonCodes, never touch another user's private event, and a retried create with the same key yields one sprk_event.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-07 (writes), FR-15, NFR-06. Task 006 moved create/complete (with ValidateCreateEventRequestAsync and RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter's checks) into IEventsCapability. Idempotent-write model: Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/CompleteDecisionTool.cs. Write-path rules: docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Tasks/CreateTaskTool.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Tasks/CompleteTaskTool.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.Tasks.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Mcp/Tasks/TaskWriteToolsTests.cs (create equals REST create; retried key → one record; complete idempotent)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/Tasks/TaskWriteToolsAuthTests.cs (other user's private event; regarding record without access)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Events/IEventsCapability.cs (task 006)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/CompleteDecisionTool.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="006" status="pending">Events capability</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">General McpToolResults</dependency>
      <dependency task="025" status="pending">Tasks ledger partial and read tools</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Run as the caller (IHttpContextAccessor; UserContextRequired; no app-only fallback). Validation and authorization are IEventsCapability's; the tools add none (spec MUST NOT copy authorization); refusals map to McpToolResults with the REST reasonCode.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">create: readOnlyHint false, destructiveHint false, idempotentHint true, required idempotencyKey; a retry with the same key and caller returns the first event id and writes nothing. complete: readOnlyHint false, destructiveHint false, idempotentHint true; completing a completed task returns success without a second write. No host consent prompt is relied on (NFR-06). Ledger rows in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.Tasks.cs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">No plugin; writes go only through IEventsCapability (one server-side owner per invariant).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Model-visible: event id, subject, due date, status, link. Logs: tool name, latency, outcome/reasonCode, correlation id; never the task description.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress.</constraint>
  </constraints>

